   "harm": "modifying core consensus/node miner logic in src/node to accommodate test-only mining behavior introduces dead code and maintenance burden",
   "hash": "034132d4b21b5556",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:42:07+00:00",
     "blocking": true,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:2083512984",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:2083512984",
   "kind": "maintenance",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "Generally, I am not sure about modifying real code to accommodate test-only code. It would be better to not modify `src/node` at all and just put the test-only code in the test-only code paths.",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2025-05-12",
    "by": "polespinasa",
    "id": "rc:2084243740",
    "quote": "Tried to follow your approach, actually it makes things easier :)"
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/32468#discussion_r2083512984"
  },
  {
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2025-05-12",
   "author": "andrewtoth",
   "author_replies": [
    "c:2873672475",
    "c:2879033872",
    "c:2907738036"
   ],
   "blocking": true,
   "fix": {
    "at": null,
    "sha": "1f1c5fd6fa177c71405fa748e8e5c5ee53b73332"
   },
   "harm": "adding a new generatetomany RPC incurs code bloat, extra test maintenance, and deprecation cycles when extending generateblock is more flexible and fixes reward fee issues",
   "hash": "e9180a1297a56175",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:42:07+00:00",
     "blocking": true,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "c:2873256932",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "c:2873256932",
   "kind": "approach",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "New RPCs require adding more code to test, and once added must go through a deprecation cycle to be removed (if they can be removed at all without disrupting too many users).",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2025-05-25",
    "by": "polespinasa",
    "id": "c:2907738036",
    "quote": "Squashed all commits and removed the first approach (`generatetomany`)"
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/32468#issuecomment-2873256932"
  },
  {
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2025-05-28",
   "author": "achow101",
   "author_replies": [
    "rc:2113587244",
    "rc:2115811246",
    "c:2922380999",
    "c:3336297423"
   ],
   "blocking": true,
   "fix": {
    "at": null,
    "sha": "1f1c5fd6fa177c71405fa748e8e5c5ee53b73332"
   },
   "harm": "requiring an array rather than continuing to accept a string breaks backwards compatibility for scripts and automated tests using generateblock",
   "hash": "b93dbcaced49b80e",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:42:07+00:00",
     "blocking": true,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:2112898168",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:2112898168",
   "kind": "interface",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "Although this RPC is only used by tests, I don't think we should be breaking backwards compatibility here. It's equally easy to determine whether this parameter is a string, so we can accept a string here for backwards compatibility.",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2025-09-26",
    "by": "polespinasa",
    "id": "c:3336297423",
    "quote": "{ \"generateblock\", 0, \"outputs\", /*also_string=*/true},"
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/32468#discussion_r2112898168"
  },
  {
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2026-03-22",
   "author": "andrewtoth",
   "author_replies": [
    "rc:2986422097"
   ],
   "blocking": false,
   "fix": {
    "at": null,
    "sha": "1f1c5fd6fa177c71405fa748e8e5c5ee53b73332"
   },
   "harm": "omitting the transaction parameter in existing functional tests changes their behavior to mine the mempool instead of generating empty blocks",
   "hash": "e7dc2749e1f90532",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:42:07+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:2971839554",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:2971839554",
   "kind": "correctness",
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "Otherwise this should be backwards compatible, and mining the mempool instead of an empty block can be a behavior change in the tests.",
   "settled_by": {
    "at": "2026-03-25",
    "by": "polespinasa",
    "id": "rc:2986422097",
    "quote": "I will add back the `transactions=[]` you are right that is a behavior change and this PR should not be changing that. Thanks."
   },
   "status": "resolved",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/32468#discussion_r2971839554"
  },
  {
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2026-04-21",
   "author": "stickies-v",
   "author_replies": [
